[TITLE] Self-monitoring of an isolated power station
[P1] On a hard-to-reach shelf, a station feeds a dispensary. It's a radio relay. The microgrid is made up of solar panels, lithium batteries and a small diesel generator. As the road may be closed for several days, a voltage meter is used. The current. temperature and vibration every 200 milliseconds. Detailed data remains in place, only a compressed summary is transmitted when the link is operational Medical and communication equipment is a priority
[P2] On 18 October 2025, a dust storm reduced solar output by 34% in fifteen minutes. The temperature of the battery cabinet rose by 8 °C, while the inverter fan produced an abnormal vibration instead of shutting down the station. The system turned off the secondary heating, reduced some of the lights, and started the rescue group. He identified three possible causes of the debris on the panels, a worn bearing, and increasing resistance in a battery connector.
[P3] After the storm, a head-mounted camera read the license plates and alarm codes, then a local processor compared them to the offline manual No sensitive images were sent to the cloud The software required the entire tag to remain within a certain margin also controlled the overall sharpness and that of the top part A voice command asked to back off if an edge was missing and four stable frames were needed. The engineers then confirmed the proposed order of cleaning the panels, replacing the bearing, and tightening the connector. The intervention lasted six minutes without interrupting a critical service reliable automation must recognize uncertainty and leave the final decision to the operator
